# Scroll chrome & sticky nav (must)

Every landing built with this pack must include theme-matched scroll UX. Do not leave browser-default chrome only.

## 1. Stylish scrollbar (theme tokens)

In `globals.css` (or equivalent):

- Track: cream / paper (`--brand-cream`)
- Thumb: gold gradient (`--brand-gold`)
- `scrollbar-width: thin` + `scrollbar-color` for Firefox
- WebKit `::-webkit-scrollbar*` for Chrome/Edge/Safari
- Hover: slightly brighter gold thumb
- `html { scroll-behavior: smooth }` with `prefers-reduced-motion: auto`

Do **not** invent purple/neon scrollbar colors. Use brand CSS vars.

## 2. Scroll-to-top control (bottom → top)

- Fixed bottom-right (`ScrollToTop` in `components/ui/`)
- Show after user leaves hero (~400px or past `#hero`)
- Brand icon (pack arrow rotated `-90deg`, or theme up-arrow)
- Ink/cream/gold circle: border gold, hover scale + gold ring
- `cursor-pointer`, focus ring, `aria-label="Scroll to top"`
- Respect reduced motion (`behavior: "auto"`)

Wire once on the landing page (or root layout) so every route benefits.

## 3. Navbar after short scroll (fixed + active bg)

- Header is `fixed` (not only `absolute`)
- At top of page: transparent / no fill
- After a small scroll (`scrollY > ~64px`): **active bg**
  - cream/ink panel at ~95% opacity
  - `backdrop-blur`
  - subtle bottom border + soft shadow
- Transition bg/border/shadow ~300ms
- Do **not** wait until the full hero leaves the viewport

## 4. Responsive (every screen)

Verify chrome at **320 · 390 · 768 · 1024 · 1280+**:

- Header: compact padding on phone; no overflow; hamburger below `lg:`
- Mobile: logo + hamburger only; menu via portal (`header-nav.mdc`)
- Scroll-to-top: smaller hit target OK on 320; keep clear of safe edges (`right-4 bottom-5`)
- Page shell: `min-w-0 max-w-full overflow-x-clip`
- Mobile menu: scrollable if long (`max-h` + `overflow-y-auto`); no horizontal page scroll

## Done check

- [ ] Themed scrollbar visible
- [ ] Scroll-to-top appears after hero, scrolls to top
- [ ] Navbar gains solid/frosted bg after a short scroll (~64px), not only after hero ends
- [ ] No horizontal scroll on phone
- [ ] Documented in `AGENTS.md` for reuse on any landing
